nner + `allow_unharnessed_subprocess` enforcement (tests/conftest.py:383), or route the new check through it instead of a parallel scanner.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["tests/_subprocess_isolation.py already AST-scans test files for spawn targets: `_SPAWN_TARGETS = frozenset({*(f\"subprocess.{n}\" for n in (\"run\", \"Popen\", \"check_output\", \"check_call\", \"call\")), \"os.system\", \"os.popen\", \"pytest.main\"})` and reports `file:line` for offending calls.","It already enforces a harness opt-out via `MARKER_NAME = \"allow_unharnessed_subprocess\"` and `unharnessed_subprocess_reason(...)`, wired into collection at tests/conftest.py:383.","The plan's guard performs the same mechanical operation (find subprocess spawn sites in tests/scripts/ and require they route through a harness, naming file+line) for the narrower target observability.sh, but the plan does not mention this existing infrastructure or argue extend-vs-rebuild.","Note: the two differ in intent (REBAR_ROOT inheritance vs. mandating run_observability specifically), so this is a coaching prompt to confirm reuse is infeasible, not an assertion of duplication."],"finding":"The plan proposes a new bespoke AST scanner in the guard test (`no test file in tests/scripts/ runs observability.sh through subprocess directly`) without checking whether the repo's existing collection-time subprocess-isolation guard can be extended to cover it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5959af99e827c39a","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 3, bullet 4 (\"no test file in tests/scripts/ runs observability.sh ... through subprocess directly ... (AST scan; names file and line)\"); AC line \"No test in tests/scripts/ runs observability.sh ... through subprocess directly; the AST guard names any file and line that does\"","norm_id":"n81b529079b740c64","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenari